> 
> I assume the -d refers to the playground, but what is base1 base2...?

     "base1" is the filename for one character's level and save files,
"base2" would the name for a second character's, and so on.  So you only
need one name to recover your own game.  It starts with a number, which
is actually your 32-bit UIC value formatted in decimal rather than the
usual pair of 16-bit octal values, followed by your character's name
(without the -? class suffix).  I don't remember whether or not you
need to precede the whole thing with an underscore; that's used in VMS
for the individual files to force the "volatile" ones to the end of the
directory, but it isn't used in the regular save file name.

$ set default hackdir
$ dir *.0
_123CONAN.0
$ mcr []recover 123CONAN        !(or perhaps _123CONAN)
should remove _123CONAN.* and create [.SAVE]123CONAN.  After that, just
resume the saved game normally.



